family: net-snmp
what: trap
transport: v2c
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: tested
reference: net-snmp manual pages: snmpd.conf(5) (trap2sink, trapsess), snmp.conf(5) (defCommunity, defSecurityName, defAuthType…), snmptrap(1)
does: Makes snmpd send its traps to Woodshed (SNMPv2c), and gives a test trap to send with snmptrap.
check: Search Events for type Traps: the trap snmpd sends at start (coldStart) and the test trap each appear once; `woodshed snmp status` counts them.
placeholders: <COMMUNITY>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- <COMMUNITY> must be one Woodshed accepts: Settings → Listeners → SNMP traps lists the communities (an empty list accepts any).
- Keep snmpd.conf readable by root only: it holds the community.
- The test trap's OID is under the documentation enterprise number (32473), so it can't be mistaken for a real alarm.
---- part file "/etc/snmp/snmpd.conf": Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv2c).
trap2sink udp:192.0.2.10:162 <COMMUNITY>
---- part file "~/.snmp/snmp.conf": For the test trap: snmptrap reads its community from this file, not the command line
defCommunity <COMMUNITY>
---- part command "": Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 2c udp:192.0.2.10:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
==== text
# /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf: Add to the agent's configuration, then restart snmpd (sudo systemctl restart snmpd); it sends a trap when it starts
# Woodshed: send traps (SNMPv2c).
trap2sink udp:192.0.2.10:162 <COMMUNITY>

# ~/.snmp/snmp.conf: For the test trap: snmptrap reads its community from this file, not the command line
defCommunity <COMMUNITY>

# Send a test trap
snmptrap -v 2c udp:192.0.2.10:162 '' 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.0.1 1.3.6.1.4.1.32473.1.1.1.0 s "Test trap for Woodshed from $(hostname)"
